#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:97
msgid ""
"Standalone Flask template with authentication, admin tools, PostgreSQL, "
"Redis, scheduled background work, and a GitLab-driven VM pipeline."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:99
msgid ""
"Use the admin menu for users, logs, and async tasks. This page summarizes"
" how the stack fits together."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:105
msgid ""
"Flask-Login sessions; passwords stored as Werkzeug hashes (scrypt or "
"pbkdf2)."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:106
msgid "Roles and permissions on the User model; admin UI under /admin."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:107
msgid ""
"The default admin account is created at startup from environment "
"variables (ADMIN_USER_*)."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:114
msgid ""
"PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy; schema changes via Alembic (see MIGRATIONS.md"
" in the repo)."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:115
msgid "Application DB name is NSFT_DB_NAME; Postgres superuser DB is POSTGRES_DB."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:116
msgid ""
"VM deployments keep data on a host volume; CI integration VMs are "
"destroyed after tests."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:122
msgid ""
"NATH_STANDALONE_FLASK_TEMPLATE_CONTEXT selects the config class in "
"lib/_config.py:"
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:126
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:127
msgid "Use"
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:131
msgid "Local Docker Compose"
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:132
msgid "CI disposable VM; TESTING enabled"
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:133
msgid "CI pre-production VM"
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:134
msgid "Production VM"
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:137
msgid ""
"Set DB_IP to the Postgres host (Compose service name or container name on"
" a VM). All deployed contexts use HTTP on port 80 behind a proxy"
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:142
msgid ""
"Background work runs inside the app process with APScheduler "
"(lib/task_scheduler.py), not a separate worker container."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:144
msgid ""
"The scheduler starts when the Flask app loads; jobs are registered with "
"register_task or the @scheduled_task decorator."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:145
msgid ""
"Cron schedules and metadata live in the scheduled_tasks table; each run "
"is logged in task_executions (status, duration, errors)."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:146
msgid ""
"Built-in job: database_backup runs daily at 04:00 (cron 0 4 * * *), "
"creates a SQL backup and prunes backups older than seven days."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:147
msgid ""
"Failed runs can trigger a Telegram alert when TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN and "
"TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID are set."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:148
msgid "Admins can inspect schedules and history under Admin → Async Tasks."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:150
msgid ""
"Add a new recurring task: define a function, decorate it with "
"@scheduled_task with a cron expression, and restart the app so "
"registration runs. Use the same pattern as database_backup in "
"task_scheduler.py."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:155
msgid ""
"GitLab CI stages: docker → integration → validation → prod. Each deployed"
" environment gets its own VM (Terraform + Pi-hole DNS + Ansible)."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:157
msgid ""
"integration: create VM, deploy, run pytest in the container, destroy VM "
"(unless INTEGRATION_KEEP_VM=true)."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:158
msgid ""
"validation: same flow after integration tests; no automated test job; "
"destroy is manual."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:159
msgid "prod: master branch only; deploy and destroy are manual."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:160
msgid "Ansible connects as user Nath; nginx listens on port 80 on every VM."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:162
msgid "CI/CD variables (project)"
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:163
msgid ""
"Set variables in GitLab → Settings → CI/CD. Shared infra vars use scope "
"*; per-env secrets use scope integration, validation, or prod."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:165
msgid ""
"PROXMOX_*, PIHOLE_*, GITLAB_CA_FILE (file), TELEGRAM_*, IP_POOL_*: not "
"protected (needed on feature branches)."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:166
msgid ""
"INTEGRATION_* and VALIDATION_*: not protected (pipelines run on merge "
"requests and feature branches)."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:167
msgid "PROD_*: protected; available on the default branch only."
msgstr ""

#: nath_standalone_flask_template/templates/doc/index.html:169
msgid ""
"Details and job graph: docs/infra_automation/ in the repository and the "
"header of .gitlab-ci.yml."
msgstr ""

